      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, that diet is risky because aged cheddar and salami contain high levels of tyramine, which can cause dangerous high blood pressure if combined with an MAOI. Similarly, fermented soy sauces can also contain trace tyramine that your new medication might interact poorly with. It's best to ask your doctor for a specific safe-food list before sticking to these items permanently.",
